The HotelBooking  smart contract acts as a trusted intermediary between the guest and the hotel owner.
When the contract is deployed, the deployer’s blockchain address becomes the owner of the contract through the Solidity msg.sender variable.
The smart contract contains mappings that storeroom prices, booking information and payments currently held in escrow.
The hotel owner can create rooms and assign booking prices using the addRoom() function. 
Guest can then select and available room and reserve it by sending the exact amount required through the payable bookRoom() function.

Unlike traditional booking systems where payments are transferred immediately to the hotel, the smart contract temporarily stores the funds.
This escrow mechanism ensure that payment is only released after the hotel confirms that the guest has checked in successfully.
If required, the guest can cancel a booking and automatically receive a refund.

Several validation checks were implemented using Solidity’s require() statements to ensure data integrity and prevent invalid transactions.
These checks verify room availability, payment accuracy and user permissions before any action can be executed.
